Apple's busiest season isn't over yet – far from it. With Black Friday kicking off this week, plus new products, software updates, and new smart home accessories running into December, there's more on the way from Apple before the end of 2026, so be sure to stick around.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2024/09/Apple-Logo-Top-Half.jpeg" alt="" width="2048" height="1152" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-968676" /><br/>
Below, we've rounded up what's still coming, along with one date in particular that's worth watching if you're a holiday shopper.<br/>
<br/>
<ul><br/>
<li><strong>Black Friday – November 27:</strong> Not a product launch unfortunately, but a date likely worth marking. Apple's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/20/apple-reveals-2026-black-friday-deals/">annual four-day shopping event</a> runs from Friday, November 27 through Monday, November 30, with gift cards worth up to &#36;300 offered with eligible purchases. Apple is also offering new and qualified returning subscribers the Apple TV streaming service for &#36;6.99 per month for six months, with that deal available until November 30. Our <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/black-friday/">Black Friday roundup</a> will be tracking all the deals.</li><br/>
<li><strong>(PRODUCT)RED AirPods Max 2 and HomePod mini 2 – expected December 1:</strong> Apple plans to release <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/24/apple-to-release-four-red-products/">(PRODUCT)RED versions</a> of the existing AirPods Max 2 and HomePod mini 2 on or around Tuesday, December 1, which is World AIDS Day, according to <em>Bloomberg</em>'s Mark Gurman. The new color is expected to be the only change. Apple is also releasing a red Wrist Strap for AirPods Pro and a red Sport Band for the Apple Watch.</li><br/>
<li><strong>App Store Awards – expected December:</strong> Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/18/2026-app-store-award-finalists/">named this year's finalists on November 18</a>, and the winners are expected in the coming weeks. Last year, Apple <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2025/12/apple-unveils-the-winners-of-the-2025-app-store-awards/">announced the winners on December 4</a>, so a similar early-December date looks likely this year.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Apple Music Replay – expected December:</strong> The full 2026 Replay recap is likely to arrive around the same time as last year's, when the full version <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/12/02/apple-music-replay-2025-fully-available/">became available on December 2</a>, with your top songs, artists, and listening stats for the year.</li><br/>
<li><strong>iOS 27.3 – December:</strong> Apple says iOS 27.3 will be released to the public <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/30/apple-says-ios-27-3-beta-coming-next-week/">in December</a>, though it hasn't given a date. The first <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/03/apple-seeds-first-ios-27-3-beta/">iOS 27.3 beta</a> arrived on Tuesday, November 3. Beta features can change before release, but so far it includes new Siri AI actions across apps, vertical tabs and an Adaptive Dark Mode in Safari, the redesigned Health app, a new Apple Fitness+ Gym Strength workout that builds a four-week plan, and more. Our <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/ios-27-3-beta-features/">iOS 27.3 beta guide</a> has the full list.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Apple Intelligence in China – December:</strong> The first Apple Intelligence features for users in China are <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/03/ios-27-3-apple-intelligence-china-2/">already in testing</a> in the iOS 27.3 beta, and Apple has <a href="https://www.apple.com.cn/newsroom/2026/10/apple-intelligence-features-are-coming-to-users-in-china/">confirmed the public rollout</a> for December alongside the update. Apple has partnered with Alibaba to add Qwen support to Siri, Writing Tools, and Visual Intelligence. The initial release is for supported iPhones, with other platforms to follow after the required regulatory approvals, and it does not include Siri AI.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Apple Home Collection – from December:</strong> The new Apple-backed, third-party lineup includes smart home cameras, thermostats, and a lock designed with LG Electronics and Schneider Electric. Apple says that availability <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/10/meet-apple-homeview-a-new-way-to-enjoy-entertainment-and-manage-the-home/">begins in December</a>, although select accessories will not arrive until early 2027.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
